    "text": "Let's denote the number of pencils Candy has as \\( C \\). According to the problem, Caleb has 3 less than twice as many pencils as Candy. Therefore, Caleb has \\( 2C - 3 \\) pencils. Calen originally had 5 more pencils than Caleb, so Calen originally had \\( (2C - 3) + 5 = 2C + 2 \\) pencils. However, Calen lost 10 pencils, so he now has \\( 2C + 2 - 10 = 2C - 8 \\) pencils. We are given that Calen now has 10 pencils, so we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 2C - 8 = 10 \\]\n\nTo find \\( C \\), we solve the equation step by step:\n\n1. Add 8 to both sides of the equation:\n\\[ 2C - 8 + 8 = 10 + 8 \\]\n\\[ 2C = 18 \\]\n\n2. Divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ \\frac{2C}{2} = \\frac{18}{2} \\]\n\\[ C = 9 \\]\n\nSo, Candy has \\(\\boxed{9}\\) pencils.",
